  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_09. Let triangle PQR be a triangle with sides PQ = 12, QR = 9, where \u2220P = 35\u00b0, \u2220Q = 65\u00b0. Let triangle XYZ be a triangle with sides YZ = 18, where \u2220Y = 80\u00b0, \u2220Z = 35\u00b0. The interior angles of triangle PQR (\u2220P, \u2220Q, \u2220R) sum to 180\u00b0. The interior angles of triangle XYZ (\u2220X, \u2220Y, \u2220Z) sum to 180\u00b0. Find the measure of \u2220X in XYZ.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A surveyor is measuring two triangular plots of land. The first plot, triangle PQR, has sides PQ = 12 meters and QR = 9 meters, with angles \u2220P = 35\u00b0 and \u2220Q = 65\u00b0. The second plot, triangle XYZ, has a side YZ = 18 meters, with angles \u2220Y = 80\u00b0 and \u2220Z = 35\u00b0.\n\nThe surveyor knows that the interior angles of any triangle must sum to 180\u00b0. Using this fact along with the given angle measures, she needs to find the measure of \u2220X in triangle XYZ so she can complete her survey records.\n\nWhat is the measure of \u2220X?"
}